---
/**
 * CURRICULUM — the PRECEPT document library, and what surrounds it.
 *
 * ═══ SOURCE — every line below is verified in this repository ══════════════
 *   PRECEPT — the school's own name for its published syllabus. One document
 *     per class, Nursery to Class XII, session 2026-27 (data/academics.ts,
 *     cited on four separate pages). Fifteen year groups; fifteen documents.
 *   The three the school names in one sentence about all its teaching:
 *     "Incorporate Technology, a theory of Multiple Intelligence and
 *      Collaborative learning in all areas of teaching."
 *   Two more from the school's own stated aims (PhilosophyStory:108-112):
 *     "Develop in children a degree of independence and self-motivation."
 *     "Encourage behavior that is tolerant, sensitive to others and reflects
 *      good manners and moral awareness."
 *     ⚠ THOSE TWO ARE WHY THE PHILOSOPHY ROW HAS FIVE CARDS AND NOT THREE. The
 *     brief asked for five; three come from the teaching sentence and two from
 *     the aims. Nothing was invented to reach the number — had the fifth not
 *     been in the school's own words, the row would have had four.
 *   Four streams after Class X — PCM · PCB · Commerce · Humanities, each taught
 *     to CBSE board level. PCM and PCB are definitional (the stream name IS the
 *     subject list); Commerce and Humanities are named without composition, and
 *     that is exactly how they are printed here.
 *   "Syllabi" is item two of twelve on the school's own Parents' Forum agenda.
 *
 * ═══ THE PRECEPT FILES ═══════════════════════════════════════════
 * All fifteen are real, and every href below was fetched and checked: 200,
 * application/pdf, over HTTPS. They live on the school’s own WordPress uploads
 * folder and are linked, not copied into this project — the client asked for
 * links, and a copy would go stale the day the school re-issues one.
 *
 * ⚠ THE SOURCE PAGE SERVES THEM OVER http://. Rewritten to https:// here after
 * confirming each one answers on it; a bare http link from an https page is a
 * mixed-content warning in the address bar of a school website.
 *
 * ⚠⚠ THE SIZES ARE ON THE CARDS BECAUSE SOME ARE ENORMOUS. Class V is 103MB,
 * Class VI 99MB, Class VII 91MB — while Class XI is under 1MB. A parent in
 * Ballia opening the wrong one on 4G deserves to know before they tap, not
 * after. Nothing can be done about the files from here; printing the number is
 * the honest minimum. The school should be told they need re-exporting.
 *
 * ⚠ href: null STILL WORKS. A class without one renders the muted issued-by-
 * the-school line instead of the action, so a withdrawn document degrades
 * rather than 404s.
 *
 * ⚠ NO DOCUMENT'S CONTENTS ARE CLAIMED. The school publishes that the documents
 * exist, one per class. It does not publish what is in them, and no subject
 * list, period allocation or assessment weighting appears anywhere here.
 *
 * ⚠ TWO RESOURCES THE BRIEF SUGGESTED ARE ABSENT: "Class Timetable" and "Text
 * Books". Neither exists in this project or on the school's site, so neither is
 * a card. The three that are cards each go somewhere real.
 *
 * ═══ COMPOSITION ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *   01 INTRO     cream · statement left, the five-stage journey right
 *   02 LIBRARY   white panel on cream · the fifteen PRECEPT cards, by stage
 *   03 PHILOSOPHY cream · five cards, each a quotation
 *   04 PATHWAYS  white · the four streams
 *   05 RESOURCES cream · three documents that exist
 *   06 CLOSE     the shared cinematic close
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { MARK } from './assessment/marks';

/**
 * The line-art books-and-cap the brief asks for behind the library.
 * ⚠ THE -cut FILE, NOT THE ORIGINAL. The supplied artwork is brown ink on a
 * WHITE ground, which on cream would have shown as a white rectangle behind the
 * panel. bookwithcap-cut.png is the same artwork with lightness converted to
 * transparency — not a flood fill, which would have stopped at the first dot of
 * the baked-in field and left it as a block. The client’s original file is
 * untouched beside it.
 */
import dBooks from '../../assets/icons/bookwithcap-cut.png';
import RichLine from '../ui/RichLine.astro';
import { getCurriculum } from '../../lib/cms';

/**
 * ⚠ A CLASS WITH NO LINK IS NOT A BROKEN LINK. With href empty the card renders
 * the muted issued-by-the-school line instead of "View PDF →" — not an anchor
 * that goes nowhere. Nothing else in the component changes.
 */
const { stages, totalDocs, one, two, three, four, five } = await getCurriculum();

/**
 * ⚠ THE CARD COLOURS ARE DESIGN, AND THEY LIVE HERE.
 *
 * Each of the three runs had a `tone` stored against every card, which meant an
 * editor adding a sixth tile had to know the palette - and a typo produced a
 * card with no colour at all. The palette belongs to the section, so the page
 * holds it and cycles it. Add a card and it takes the next colour.
 */
const PHILOSOPHY_TONES = ['sky', 'lilac', 'mint', 'sun', 'rose'];
const STREAM_TONES = ['sky', 'mint', 'peach', 'lilac'];
const RESOURCE_TONES = ['peach', 'sky', 'mint'];
const toneOf = (palette, i) => palette[i % palette.length];


---

<div class="cu">
  {/* ═══ 01 · ONE CURRICULUM, EVERY STAGE ════════════════════════════════════ */}
  <section class="cu-intro" aria-labelledby="cu-intro-h">
    <span class="cu__dots cu__dots--tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="u-container cu-intro__in">
      <div class="cu-intro__copy">
        <p class="cu__k t-label" data-reveal>{one.kicker}</p>
        <h2 class="cu-intro__h" id="cu-intro-h" data-split>
          {one.heading}<br /><em>{one.headingEm}</em>
        </h2>
        <RichLine class="cu__p" text={one.body[0]} reveal revealDelay={150} />
        <span class="cu__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>

      {/* ⚠ AN <ol>, NOT A ROW OF DIVS. Nursery → Class XII is an order, and a
          screen reader should hear it as one. The connectors are drawn between
          steps with a pseudo-element rather than as elements of their own. */}
      <ol class="cu-journey">
        {stages.map((s, i) => (
          <li class="cu-journey__step" data-pop data-pop-delay={i * 90}>
            <span class="cu-journey__m" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" set:html={MARK[s.mark]} />
              </svg>
            </span>
            <span class="cu-journey__k">{s.label}</span>
            <span class="cu-journey__v">{s.range}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ═══ 02 · THE LIBRARY ════════════════════════════════════════════════════
      The centrepiece. Fifteen classes in five stage rows, on one raised panel
      over the cream so the whole library reads as a single object. */}
  <section class="cu-lib" aria-labelledby="cu-lib-h">
    <span class="cu__grid" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="cu-lib__ghost" aria-hidden="true">PRECEPT</span>

    <div class="u-container">
      <div class="cu-lib__panel">
        {/* Decorative only — aria-hidden, and it sits behind the panel. The parallax
            is deliberately small: the brief asks for decoration that moves very
            subtly, not for the illustration to travel across the section. */}
        <Image
          class="cu-lib__art"
          src={dBooks}
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          widths={[280, 560]}
          sizes="380px"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          data-parallax
          data-parallax-y="-26"
        />

        <header class="cu-lib__head">
          <p class="cu__k t-label" data-reveal>{two.kicker}</p>
          <h2 class="cu-lib__h" id="cu-lib-h" data-split>{two.heading}</h2>
          <span class="cu__rule cu__rule--mid" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </header>

        {stages.map((s) => (
          <div class="cu-row">
            <div class="cu-row__stage" data-reveal>
              <span class="cu-row__m" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" set:html={MARK[s.mark]} />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <span class="cu-row__t">
                <span class="cu-row__k">{s.label}</span>
                <span class="cu-row__v">{s.blurb}</span>
              </span>
            </div>

            <ul class="cu-row__cards">
              {s.classes.map((c, i) => (
                <li>
                  {/* ⚠ AN <a> ONLY WHERE A FILE EXISTS. With href null this is a
                      plain card — not a link that goes nowhere, and not a button
                      that does nothing. */}
                  {c.href ? (
                    <a class="cu-card cu-card--live" href={c.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-reveal data-reveal-delay={i * 60}>
                      <span class="cu-card__k">{c.label}</span>
                      <span class="cu-card__tag">PRECEPT</span>
                      <span class="cu-card__go">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                          <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" set:html={MARK.doc} />
                        </svg>
                        View PDF{c.sizeMb ? ` · ${c.sizeMb} MB` : ''}
                        <svg class="cu-card__arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                          <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" set:html={MARK.arrow} />
                        </svg>
                      </span>
                    </a>
                  ) : (
                    <div class="cu-card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay={i * 60}>
                      <span class="cu-card__k">{c.label}</span>
                      <span class="cu-card__tag">PRECEPT</span>
                      <span class="cu-card__go cu-card__go--pending">
                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                          <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" set:html={MARK.doc} />
                        </svg>
                        Issued by the school
                      </span>
                    </div>
                  )}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}

        {/* ⚠ THE PANEL SAYS OUT LOUD WHY THERE IS NO DOWNLOAD, rather than
            leaving a parent to click fifteen cards and find out. */}
        {/* The count in this sentence is filled in from how many classes there
            actually are, so it cannot disagree with the cards above it. */}
        <RichLine class="cu-lib__note" text={two.body[0]} reveal />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ═══ 03 · PHILOSOPHY ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */}
  <section class="cu-phil" aria-labelledby="cu-phil-h">
    <div class="u-container cu-phil__in">
      <div class="cu-phil__lede">
        <p class="cu__k t-label" data-reveal>{three.kicker}</p>
        <h2 class="cu-phil__h" id="cu-phil-h" data-split>
          {three.heading}<br /><em>{three.headingEm}</em>
        </h2>
      </div>

      <ul class="cu-phil__set">
        {three.tiles.map((p, i) => (
          <li class="cu-tile" data-reveal data-reveal-delay={i * 80}>
            <span class={`cu-tile__m tone tone--${toneOf(PHILOSOPHY_TONES, i)}`} aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" set:html={MARK[p.mark]} />
              </svg>
            </span>
            <span class="cu-tile__k">{p.label}</span>
            <span class="cu-tile__v">{p.value}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ═══ 04 · PATHWAYS ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */}
  <section class="cu-path" aria-labelledby="cu-path-h">
    <div class="u-container cu-path__in">
      <div class="cu-path__lede">
        <p class="cu__k t-label" data-reveal>{four.kicker}</p>
        <h2 class="cu-path__h" id="cu-path-h" data-split>
          {four.heading}<br /><em>{four.headingEm}</em>
        </h2>
      </div>

      <ul class="cu-path__set">
        {four.tiles.map((s, i) => (
          <li class="cu-stream" data-reveal data-reveal-delay={i * 80}>
            <span class={`cu-stream__m tone tone--${toneOf(STREAM_TONES, i)}`} aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" set:html={MARK[s.mark]} />
              </svg>
            </span>
            <span class="cu-stream__k">{s.label}</span>
            <span class="cu-stream__v">{s.value}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ═══ 05 · RESOURCES ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */}
  <section class="cu-res" aria-labelledby="cu-res-h">
    <div class="u-container cu-res__in">
      <div class="cu-res__lede">
        <p class="cu__k t-label" data-reveal>{five.kicker}</p>
        <h2 class="cu-res__h" id="cu-res-h" data-split>{five.heading}</h2>
      </div>

      <ul class="cu-res__set">
        {five.tiles.map((r, i) => (
          <li data-reveal data-reveal-delay={i * 80}>
            <a
              class="cu-doc"
              href={r.href}
              target={r.isFile ? '_blank' : undefined}
              rel={r.isFile ? 'noopener noreferrer' : undefined}
            >
              <span class={`cu-doc__m tone tone--${toneOf(RESOURCE_TONES, i)}`} aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" set:html={MARK[r.mark]} />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <span class="cu-doc__t">
                <span class="cu-doc__k">{r.label}</span>
                <span class="cu-doc__v">{r.value}</span>
              </span>
              <span class="cu-doc__go" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
                  <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" set:html={MARK.arrow} />
                </svg>
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .cu { position: relative; }

  .cu-intro,
  .cu-lib,
  .cu-phil,
  .cu-path,
  .cu-res {
    position: relative;
    overflow: clip;
  }

  .cu__k { color: var(--sb-violet); }

  /* Body holds at 16.5px on a wide screen and floors at 15 — the offset form,
     not a bare vw, so a 1440 laptop actually reaches the top of the range. */
  :global(.cu__p) {
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin: clamp(12px, 1.5vw, 17px) 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 0.5vw + 9px, 16.5px);
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--sb-text-secondary);
  }
  :global(.cu__p strong) { font-weight: 700; color: var(--sb-charcoal); }
  :global(.cu__p em) { font-style: italic; color: var(--sb-charcoal); }

  .cu__rule {
    display: block;
    width: 48px;
    height: 3px;
    margin: clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 26px) 0 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--sb-violet);
  }
  .cu__rule--mid { margin-inline: auto; }

  /* Shared heading shape; `em` is the orange half of every statement here. */
  .cu-intro__h,
  .cu-lib__h,
  .cu-phil__h,
  .cu-path__h,
  .cu-res__h {
    margin: clamp(9px, 1.1vw, 14px) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.024em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .cu-intro__h em,
  .cu-phil__h em,
  .cu-path__h em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--sb-violet);
  }

  /* ⚠ 52px CAP. The brief asked for 48–60 on the major heading and warned off
     80–100px; the offset middle term reaches the cap by ~1440 instead of
     idling at 40 on the commonest desktop width there is. */
  .cu-intro__h { font-size: clamp(28px, 1.9vw + 21px, 54px); }
  .cu-lib__h { font-size: clamp(25px, 1.2vw + 18px, 42px); }
  .cu-phil__h,
  .cu-path__h,
  .cu-res__h { font-size: clamp(23px, 1.2vw + 16px, 38px); }

  /* ═══ 01 · INTRO ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .cu-intro {
    background: var(--sb-ivory);
    padding-block: clamp(44px, 5.6vw, 88px);
  }
  .cu-intro__in {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.86fr) minmax(0, 1.14fr);
    gap: clamp(30px, 4.4vw, 74px);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .cu__dots {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 0;
    width: clamp(120px, 15vw, 220px);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    background-image: radial-gradient(color-mix(in srgb, var(--sb-orange-bright) 46%, transparent) 1.5px, transparent 1.5px);
    background-size: 14px 14px;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .cu__dots--tr {
    top: -3%;
    right: -2%;
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(220deg, #000 6%, transparent 74%);
    mask-image: linear-gradient(220deg, #000 6%, transparent 74%);
  }

  /* ⚠ THE CONNECTOR IS A PSEUDO-ELEMENT ON EACH STEP BUT THE LAST, drawn from
     the icon's own row so it passes BETWEEN the circles rather than through
     them. A single line behind the row cannot do that. */
  .cu-journey {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(4px, 0.8vw, 12px);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .cu-journey__step {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .cu-journey__step:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: calc(clamp(46px, 4.4vw, 62px) / 2);
    left: calc(50% + clamp(46px, 4.4vw, 62px) / 2 + 7px);
    right: calc(-50% + clamp(46px, 4.4vw, 62px) / 2 - 7px);
    height: 1px;
    background-image: linear-gradient(to right, color-mix(in srgb, var(--sb-orange-bright) 60%, transparent) 0 5px, transparent 5px 11px);
    background-size: 11px 1px;
    background-repeat: repeat-x;
  }
  .cu-journey__m {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: clamp(46px, 4.4vw, 62px);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--sb-orange-bright) 42%, transparent);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--sb-paper);
    color: var(--sb-violet);
    box-shadow: 0 10px 22px -14px rgba(28, 14, 8, 0.3);
  }
  .cu-journey__m svg { width: 46%; height: auto; }
  .cu-journey__k {
    margin-top: 4px;
    font-size: clamp(8.6px, 0.68vw, 10.5px);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sb-violet);
  }
  .cu-journey__v {
    font-size: clamp(11px, 0.82vw, 13px);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--sb-text-secondary);
  }

  /* ═══ 02 · LIBRARY ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .cu-lib {
    background: var(--sb-ivory);
    padding-block: 0 clamp(44px, 5.6vw, 84px);
  }
  .cu__grid {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    background-image:
      radial-gradient(color-mix(in srgb, var(--sb-orange-bright) 30%, transparent) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 22px 22px;
    /* Shifted off the books illustration below — two dot fields stacked in one
       corner read as a printing error rather than as decoration. */
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(58% 44% at 90% 34%, #000 8%, transparent 74%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(58% 44% at 90% 34%, #000 8%, transparent 74%);
  }
  .cu-lib__ghost {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    bottom: 2%;
    z-index: 0;
    translate: -50% 0;
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(74px, 13vw, 190px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.8;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    color: rgba(27, 21, 18, 0.032);
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* ⚠⚠ INSIDE THE PANEL, NOT BEHIND IT. Anchored to the section it sat almost
     entirely under the panel — the panel is opaque white, so all but the last
     80px was simply invisible. The short rows (Secondary is two cards, Senior
     Secondary two) leave a real hole at the panel’s bottom-right, and that hole
     is where the reference puts this illustration. z-index 0 against the rows’
     1 keeps it behind the cards it tucks under. */
  .cu-lib__art {
    position: absolute;
    right: clamp(-16px, -0.6vw, -4px);
    bottom: clamp(58px, 7vw, 104px);
    z-index: 0;
    width: clamp(180px, 24vw, 340px);
    height: auto;
    opacity: 0.62;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .cu-lib__panel {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    overflow: clip;
    padding: clamp(26px, 3.4vw, 52px) clamp(18px, 2.6vw, 40px);
    border: 1px solid var(--sb-border);
    border-radius: var(--sb-r-3);
    background: var(--sb-paper);
    box-shadow: 0 36px 78px -46px rgba(28, 14, 8, 0.34);
  }
  .cu-lib__head { position: relative; z-index: 1; text-align: center; margin-bottom: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px); }

  /* ⚠ THE STAGE LABEL IS A COLUMN, NOT A ROW HEADING ABOVE THE CARDS. Keeping
     it beside its classes is what lets a parent scan down the left edge for
     their child's stage and read straight across — the whole point of the
     library. It becomes a row heading only when the grid stacks. */
  .cu-row {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: clamp(140px, 15vw, 178px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(10px, 1.4vw, 18px);
    margin-bottom: clamp(10px, 1.4vw, 18px);
  }
  .cu-row__stage {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(8px, 1vw, 13px);
    padding: clamp(12px, 1.5vw, 18px);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--sb-orange-bright) 22%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--sb-r-2);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sb-orange-bright) 5%, transparent);
  }
  .cu-row__m {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: clamp(30px, 2.8vw, 38px);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--sb-orange-bright) 40%, transparent);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--sb-paper);
    color: var(--sb-violet);
  }
  .cu-row__m svg { width: 52%; height: auto; }
  .cu-row__t { display: grid; gap: 2px; min-width: 0; }
  .cu-row__k {
    font-size: clamp(9px, 0.7vw, 10.5px);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sb-violet);
  }
  .cu-row__v {
    font-size: clamp(11px, 0.82vw, 12.5px);
